From 7dcc4345ef58bb8102173865be52393d67d873e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: u <u@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:02:14 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 12/27] arm64: user: window/dialog/message thunks and 64-bit
 window longs (WIP)

- TIMERTHUNK, DLGPROCTHUNK and the edit word break thunks use
  NATIVE_CLOSURE on aarch64.
- WINPROC_THUNK (16-bit code) pushes the winproc handle on 64-bit;
  the real window procedure is kept in thunk_procs.
- 16-bit DWL_* offsets (DWL_*16) are distinct from DWLP_* on 64-bit.
- Pointer sized window/class values use the *Ptr functions.
- Dialog item creation data holds a 4-byte SEGPTR.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
